hadiths[36]{hadithnumber,text}:
"452","Kharijab bin Hudhafah narrated:\Allah's Messenger came out to us and he said: 'Indeed Allah has assisted you with a Salat that is better for you than red camels: Al-Witr which Allah made for you between the Isha prayer till Al-Fajr has begun"""
"453","Ali said:""Al-Witr is not incumbent like your obligatory prayers, but it is a Sunnah of Allah's Messenger who said: ""Indeed Allah is Witr (One), and He loves Al-Witr, so perform Al-Witr O people of the Qur'an"
"454","Abū Kurayb narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us, Abū Isḥāq narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah, from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: \Witr is not an obligation (ḥatm) like your prescribed prayers"
"455","Abu Hurairah narrated:\\n\\n Allah's Messenger ordered me to perform Al-Witr before sleeping. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 455 Arabic Hadees: 455\""456"""
"456","Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us from Isra'il, from Isa ibn Abi Azzah, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Thawr al-Azdi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to perform witr before I sleep. Isa ibn Abi Azzah said: Al-Sha'bi used to perform witr in the early part of the night, then sleep. He said: In this chapter there is a narration from Abu Dharr. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Abu Hurayrah is hasan gharib from this route. Abu Thawr al-Azdi's name is Habib ibn Abi Mulaykah. A group of people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and those after them chose that the man should not sleep until he performs witr. It has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: ""Whoever among you fears that he will not wake up at the end of the night, let him perform witr at its beginning; and whoever hopes to stand at the end of the night, let him perform witr at its end, for the recitation of the Qur'an at the end of the night is witnessed, and it is better."" Hannad narrated this to us: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir from the Prophet ﷺ to that effect."
"457","Umm Salamah narrated:\\n\\n The Prophet would perform Witr with thirteen [Rak'ah]. When he was older and became weak he performed Witr with seven. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 457 Arabic Hadees: 457\""458"""
"458","Hannad narrated to us: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Yahya al-Jazzar, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Prophet ﷺ used to perform witr with thirteen rak'ahs; when he grew old and weak, he performed witr with seven. He said: In this chapter there is a narration from Aishah. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Umm Salamah is hasan. It has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ regarding witr: thirteen, eleven, nine, seven, five, three, and one. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim said: The meaning of what is narrated that the Prophet ﷺ used to perform witr with thirteen is that he used to pray thirteen rak'ahs of the night including the witr, so the night prayer was attributed to the witr. He narrated a hadith regarding this from Aishah and cited as evidence what is narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: ""Perform witr, O people of the Qur'an."" He said: He only meant by it the standing of the night, saying: ""The standing of the night is only upon the people of the Qur'an."""
"459","Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from his father, from Aishah, who said: The prayer of the Prophet ﷺ at night was thirteen rak'ahs; he would perform witr from that with five, not sitting in any of them except the last. When the mu'adhdhin called the adhan, he stood and prayed two light rak'ahs. He said: In this chapter there is a narration from Abu Ayyub. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Aishah is hasan sahih. Some people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others saw witr with five, and said: He does not sit in any of them except the last. Abu Isa said: I asked Abu Mus'ab al-Madini about this hadith: ""The Prophet ﷺ used to perform witr with nine and seven."" I said: ""How does he perform witr with nine and seven?"" He said: ""He prays two by two, gives salam, and performs witr with one."""
"460","Hannad narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Prophet ﷺ used to perform witr with three, reciting in them nine surahs from al-Mufassal, reciting in each rak'ah three surahs, the last of them being ""Say: He is Allah, the One"" (112). He said: In this chapter there are narrations from Imran ibn Husayn, Aishah, Ibn Abbas, Abu Ayyub. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and it is also narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from the Prophet ﷺ. Thus some narrated it without mentioning Ubayy, and some mentioned it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from Ubayy. Abu Isa said: A group of people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others went to this and saw that the man should perform witr with three. Sufyan said: ""If you wish, perform witr with five; if you wish, with three; if you wish, with one."" Sufyan said: ""What I prefer is to perform witr with three rak'ahs."" This is the view of Ibn al-Mubarak and the people of Kufa. Sa'id ibn Yaqub al-Talqani narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Hisham from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: ""They used to perform witr with five, with three, and with one, and they saw all of that as good."""
"461","Anas bin Sirin narrated that :he asked Ibn Umar about the length of the two Rak'ah (before) Al-Fajr. He said: \The Prophet would pray two and two during the night"""
"462","Ibn Abbas narrated:\Allah's Messenger would recite during Al-Witr: \""Glorify the Name of your Lord the Most High' and"""
"463","Abdul-Aziz bin Juraij said:\I asked Aishah about what (recitation) Allah's Messenger would perform Al-Witr with. She said: 'In the first he would recite: Glorify the Name of your Lord the Most High"""
"464","Al-Hasan bin Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] said:\Allah's Messenger taught me some phrases to say during Al-Witr (Allahummahdini fiman hadait"""
"465","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever sleeps past Al-Witr or forgets it"""
"466","Zaid bin Aslam narrated from his father that:the Prophet said: \Whoever sleeps past his Al-Witr then let him pray it in the morning"""
"467","Ibn Umar narrated that :the Prophet said: \Precede the morning with Al-Witr"""
"468","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Perform Witr before the morning comes upon you"""
"469","Ibn Umar narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: ""When Fajr begins, then every Salat of the night and Al-Witr have gone, so perform Al-Witr before Fajr begins"
"470","Qais bin Talq bin Ali narrated that :his father said: I heard Allah's Messenger saying: \There are no two Witr in one night"""
"471","Umm Salamah narrated:\The Prophet would pray two Rak'ah after Al-Witr"""
"472","Sa'eed bin Yasar narrated:\I was with Ibn Umar on a journey and I fell behind him. He said: 'Where were you?' I said: 'I prayed Al-Witr.' He said: 'Is there not a good exampled for you in Allah's Messenger? I saw Allah's Messenger performing Al-Witr on his mount"""
"473","Anas bin Malik narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever prays twelve Rak'ah of Ad-Duha"""
"474","Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Laila narrated:\No one informed that they saw Allah's Messenger praying Ad-Duha except Umm Hani. She narrated that Allah's Messenger entered her house on the Day of the Conquest of Makkah. He performed Ghusl and performed eight voluntary Rak'ah such that she had not ever seen him pray any Salat lighter than them"""
"475","Abū Jaʿfar al-Simnānī narrated to us, Abū Mushir narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Baḥīr ibn Saʿd, from Khālid ibn Maʿdān, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abū al-Dardāʾ and Abū Dharr, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he reported from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, who said: \O son of Adam"
"476","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever continuously performs the two Rak'ah of Ad-Duha his sins will be forgiven"""
"477","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated:\The Prophet would pray Ad-Duha until we would say: 'He will not leave it.' And he would leave it until we would say: 'He will not pray it"""
"478","Abdullah bin As-Sa'ib narrated:\Allah's Messenger would pray four (Rak'ah) after the Zawal of the sun before Az-Zuhr. He said: 'It is an hour in which the gates of the heavens are opened"""
"479","Abdullah bin Abi Awfa narrated that :Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: \Whoever has a need from Allah"""
"480","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:\Allah's Messenger would teach us Al-Isthikhara for all of our affairs just as he would teach us a Surah of the Qur'an"""
"481","Anas bin Malik narrated that :Umm Sulaim came upon the Prophet and said: \Teach me some words that I can say in my Salat.\"" So he said: \""Mention Allah's Greatness (saying: Allahu Akbar) ten times"""
"482","Abu Rafi narrated that :Allah's Messenger said to Al-Abbas: \O uncle! Shall I not give to you"""
"483","Ka'b bin Ujrah narrated:\We said: 'O Messenger of Allah! We have learned about saying the Salam to you"""
"484","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \The person closest to me on the Day of Judgement is the one who sent the most Salat upon me"""
"485","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever sends Salat upon me"""
"486","Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated:\Indeed the supplication stops between the heavens and the earth. Nothing of it is raised up until you send Salat upon your Prophet"""
"487","Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him] said:\No one should sell in our markets except one who has understanding in the religion"""
